Task 4: Binary Classification and Model Evaluation 

Project Goal:
To implement and thoroughly evaluate foundational classification models (Logistic Regression and K-Nearest Neighbors) for a binary prediction task (e.g., predicting customer churn or medical diagnosis).

Key Outcomes & Skills:
a. Classification Implementation: Trained a Logistic Regression model, interpreting its probability output for binary outcomes. Also implemented K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), demonstrating understanding of non-parametric methods.

b. Deep Evaluation: Utilized the Confusion Matrix to break down classification performance (True Positives, False Negatives) and reported on Precision, Recall, and F1-Score, prioritizing metrics based on the business context (e.g., minimizing False Negatives).

c. Performance Visualization: Generated the Receiver Operating Characteristic (ROC) Curve and calculated the Area Under the Curve (AUC) to assess the model's discriminative power across various probability thresholds.

d. Hyperparameter Selection: Optimized the KNN model by selecting the optimal k value using cross-validation.

Technical Stack:
Category: Tool / Concept
Libraries: Scikit-learn (LogisticRegression, KNeighborsClassifier)
Concepts: Binary Classification, Confusion Matrix, Precision/Recall/F1-Score, AUC-ROC, K-Fold Cross-Validation
